silo uninstall: project silo-test-project

  tenants           ok      / no silo but the root, and no facade objects or agents in it
  orphans           ok      no object with a silo's label or prefix that silod doesn't know
  credentials       ok      no agent credentials, and no control VM holds silo-credential-key
  admin             ok      nobody holds roles/iap.tunnelResourceAccessor on silo-control
  control           delete  silo-control in us-central1-a
  migrate           ok      no silo-migrate
  db-endpoint       delete  silo-db t3st.us-central1.sql.goog.
                            silo-db-psc (forwarding rule)
                            silo-db-psc (address) 10.255.254.2
  image             delete  silo and its silod images
  dns               delete  silo.internal. A 10.255.255.2
                            silo-internal
  address           delete  silo-gateway-ip 10.255.255.2
  fence             delete  silo-fence
  nat               delete  silo-router and silo-gateway-nat
  control-subnet    delete  silo-ctl
  gateway-subnet    delete  silo-gateway
  network           delete  silo
  role              delete  projects/silo-test-project/roles/silod bound to silod
                            roles/logging.logWriter bound to silod
                            roles/artifactregistry.reader bound to silod
                            projects/silo-test-project/roles/silod
  service-account   delete  silod@silo-test-project.iam.gserviceaccount.com
  db-instance       delete  silo-db-t3st deletion protection lifted on this instance only, then
                            deleted, with every grant, policy and audit record in it, and its IAM
                            user; a final backup is kept 30 days
  apis              keep    leaves on artifactregistry, cloudbilling, cloudquotas,
                            cloudresourcemanager, compute, dns, iam, iap, logging, serviceusage,
                            sqladmin
                            why: uninstall doesn't disable APIs: something else in the project may
                            use them

  19 steps: 13 to delete, 1 to keep, 5 ok
  Estimated time: about 7 minutes, most of it waiting for Cloud SQL.
